@startuml GitEasyDeployment
title GitEasy - Deployment View (v1.5.5)
skinparam shadowing false

node "User workstation" {
  component "PowerShell session\n(PS 5.1 or PS 7)" as PSSession
  component "GitEasy module\n(GitEasy.psd1 + GitEasy.psm1)" <<command>> as Module
  component "git.exe\n(hard runtime dep)" <<boundary>> as Git
  component "Credential stores\nGCM / Windows Vault / SSH agent" <<store>> as Creds
  database "%LOCALAPPDATA%\\GitEasy\\Logs\\\n(one .log per invocation;\n30-day auto-prune)" <<store>> as Logs
  file "Temp commit/tag message file\n(GUID-named; deleted in finally)" <<store>> as TempFile
}

database ".git repository\n(local filesystem)" <<store>> as LocalRepo

cloud "Network remote\ngithub.com / gitlab.com" <<boundary>> as Remote

PSSession --> Module : loads
Module --> Git : all git work routes\nthrough Invoke-GEGit (single point)
Git --> LocalRepo : read / write
Git --> Remote : fetch (read) / push (write)\nHTTPS or SSH
Module --> Creds : Set-Token / Set-Ssh /\nSet-Vault write;\nTest-Login / Get-VaultStatus read
Module --> Logs : write one log per invocation;\nAdd-GELogStep appends per git step
Module --> TempFile : Save-Work and New-Release\nwrite here; deleted after git call

note bottom of Module
  No PowerShell module imports at runtime.\ngit.exe is the only hard runtime dependency.
end note
@enduml
